<BaseLayout title="Travel Insurance Cost Calculator — Quote-Based Budget Planner" description="Add quoted travel-insurance costs without assuming a modelled premium is an insurer’s offer."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Travel Insurance Cost Calculator</h1><p class="mb-8">Add quoted travel-insurance costs without assuming a modelled premium is an insurer’s offer.</p><Calculator client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Use your actual quotes</h2><p>Get a quote for your age, destination, trip dates and medical circumstances. Enter the premium and any separate optional cover or service cost. If the quote already includes a charge, enter zero in the separate row to avoid counting it twice.</p><h2>Check cover as well as price</h2><p>Read exclusions, deductibles, emergency assistance, repatriation, territorial cover and policy dates. A visa requirement and a policy’s benefits are different matters. The tool cannot establish whether an insurer or policy is accepted by a consulate.</p><h2>Understand the result</h2><p>Per-person rows are multiplied by the traveller count; shared rows are added once. The total is divided by the number of travellers for the average per-person budget. Changing currency clears amounts because this planner does not convert prices.</p><p>For example, a shared transfer of 10,000 in the selected currency is 10,000 for the group, not 10,000 for every person. Check whether your supplier quotes per room, per traveller or for the whole group before entering a number.</p><h2>Keep a planning record</h2><p>Save the supplier name, quote date, validity, inclusions and cancellation terms with your budget. Enter zero where a cost does not apply. No unverified default fares, visa prices or insurance premiums are supplied here.</p><p>Use our <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">visa fee service</a> and <a href="/guides/">travel guides</a> for the next checks. Calculations remain in your browser.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
